WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.509
If you want to hear about the disturbing details
of the Bowers Gang that were too dark for

00:00:03.509 --> 00:00:06.540
the movie, then stick around to the end of
this video.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.679
One of the things that makes Stephen King’s
fictional town of Derry, Maine so frightening

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:18.340
is that it’s sewer dwelling clown isn’t
the only monster that the kids have to deal

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:23.550
with -- the city is also filled with human
monsters, and many of them come from Henry

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.840
Bowers's Gang of bullies.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.410
My name is Professor CZsWorld and today on
Horror History, we’re going to dissect the

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.550
messed up minds of the young tyrants of Derry’s
streets, so let’s take it back to the beginning

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.640
with the birth of Henry Bowers.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.712
Henry is born in the year 1946.

00:00:38.712 --> 00:00:41.550
He is the son of Oscar Bowers, also known
as Butch.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.820
I think Henry’s evil tendencies took foot
from an early age as a result of his parents.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.870
His father was a mentally unstable farmer,
who physically abused his wife and son, so

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:52.100
Henry’s mother left the family at a young
age.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.310
Butch eventually started dating a woman named
Rena Davenport.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:59.620
Since Butch was often at odds with his African-American
neighbor Will Hanlon, I think Henry picked

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:03.400
up the same racist tendencies and took things
out on Will’s son Mike.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.380
Every single member of the Losers Club believed
that Henry despised them the most, but if

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.560
you were to ask Henry, he’d say Mike is
the one that really draws his ire.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.100
I mean I don’t think he’d put it so eloquently,
but you get the idea.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:19.049
When he was younger, Henry killed the Hanlon’s
dog Mr. Chips by feeding him a poisoned burger

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:23.049
-- and I think the key to understanding this
horrible act, is the fact that Henry was proud

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.069
as he presented what he had done to his father.

00:01:25.069 --> 00:01:27.939
The environment he was raised in really impacted
his actions.

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:31.819
The kids in Derry often seem to agree that
when Henry’s father takes things out on

00:01:31.819 --> 00:01:35.389
him, Henry, in turn, vents his frustrations
into the other kids of Derry.

00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:38.560
Henry terrorizes the Loser’s Club with his
own gang of bullies.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.479
When he was 6, he met Victor Criss who joins
up with Henry mostly out of fear.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:46.020
Victor was the closest thing the Bowers gang
had to intelligence or morality.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.270
He seemed more interested in frightening their
victims than hurting them, kind of like how

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:53.280
I feel about my viewers, and as the summer
progressed, it seems like he becomes more

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.549
aware of Henry’s deteriorating sanity than
anyone else.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:00.169
Henry and Vic could usually be found with
Reginald Huggins, who goes by the moniker

00:02:00.169 --> 00:02:01.170
Belch because

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.170
*burp*

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.840
*burp*

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.600
Well, yeah, because of that.

00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:09.599
These three were the main core of the Bowers
Gang, but would sometimes be joined by others,

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:13.379
such as Patrick Hockstetter -- who was maybe
more disturbed than Henry himself.

00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:17.480
Alhough Patrick was quiet and kept to himself,
he would partake in the collection of dead

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:22.049
animals, he touched his classmates in inappropriate
ways and killed his baby brother out of jealousy,

00:02:22.049 --> 00:02:25.290
an event he discovered a sense of arousal
towards violence from.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:29.360
Other members of Henry’s Gang include Peter
Gordon, a rich kid who joins Bowers’ Gang

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.579
to boost his reputation; Steve “Moose”
Sadler, a big strong kid, as his nickname

00:02:33.579 --> 00:02:37.469
implies, who was likely coerced into joining
because he’s a bit mentally handicapped

00:02:37.469 --> 00:02:41.489
and Henry probably takes advantage of him;
and Gard Jagermeyer, a big slow kid who was

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:45.110
described as being so stupid they didn’t
even both sending him to summer school.

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:48.370
I definitely need to steal that insult in
the future -- I ****ing love that.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:52.330
At the end of the 1958 school year, Henry
is in danger of having to do a little summer

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.379
school himself.

00:02:53.379 --> 00:02:56.969
Again, this is something that scares him because
he’s supposed to help his dad on the farm

00:02:56.969 --> 00:03:00.709
during the summer, so his father will probably
beat him if he has to go to summer school

00:03:00.709 --> 00:03:01.709
instead.

00:03:01.709 --> 00:03:04.459
He tries taking his academic frustrations
out on his classmates.

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:08.090
He goes after Richie Tozier, a common target
of his because of his loud mouth.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:11.610
One day at school, Richie called him “banana
heels” when Henry slipped on a puddle.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.850
Belch was the one to notice Richie trying
to sneak away after the last bell, and they

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:17.660
chased him all the way through town to Freese's
department store.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:21.340
Henry had the intention of seriously hurting
Richie, and Richie was only able to get away

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:25.010
after hiding in the toy department and sneaking
out the emergency exit.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:28.780
During the last exam of the year, Henry asks
Ben Hanscom to let him copy his work, but

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.280
Ben turns him down, causing Henry to fail
the test.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.910
On the last day of school, Henry gathers Victor
and Belch to get his revenge.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.889
They search Derry and eventually find Ben
going into the library.

00:03:37.889 --> 00:03:41.269
The three wait for him to come out and follow
him until he’s out of sight.

00:03:41.269 --> 00:03:44.739
Victor and Belch seize him, and Henry pulls
out his blade, telling Ben he’s going to

00:03:44.739 --> 00:03:48.379
carve his name into Ben’s gut so that he
never forgets to let him copy.

00:03:48.379 --> 00:03:50.430
Again -- not exactly the smartest thing to
do.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:54.109
I mean, if any of you are planning on committing a
crime tonight, I’d urge you not to inscribe

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:57.439
your real name as evidence, but that’s just
my advice, take it or leave it.

00:03:57.439 --> 00:04:00.409
Victor didn’t think Henry was actually going
to go through with it, but after carving the

00:04:00.409 --> 00:04:04.450
letter H, Ben pushes back against him and
sends himself tumbling into the Barrens, where

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.489
Henry goes chasing after in a rage.

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:08.750
Ben then trips him and kicks him in the balls.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:09.750
"AHHH!!!!"

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.420
Henry sends Victor and Belch after him, but
instead, they end up finding Bill and Eddie,

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.249
who are attempting to build a dam in the stream.

00:04:15.249 --> 00:04:18.449
When Henry joins back up with them, he does
what his father would have done, and takes

00:04:18.449 --> 00:04:22.389
his frustrations out on them and their dam,
breaking Eddie’s nose and sending him into

00:04:22.389 --> 00:04:23.500
an asthma attack.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:27.920
Henry, Victor and Belch would continue looking
for Ben around town all day before eventually

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:30.800
giving up and getting on bus back towards
Henry’s house.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:34.240
As the summer progresses, Henry becomes crazier
and more violent.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.120
One Saturday in June, Henry and the gang go
to the Aladdin theater for a movie, and on

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.660
the way there, nearly cross paths again with
Ben Hanscom, causing Ben to hide until they

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:43.660
pass by.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:47.050
In the mini-series, the Losers spill concessions
on the bullies, but in the book, they try

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.780
to sneak out a side door after Victor and
Henry look up and see them on the balcony.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:54.590
The Bowers Gang trapped them in the alley
with Henry, Victor and Belch on one side and

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:58.280
two other unnamed thugs, most likely Moose
and Jagermeyer, on the other.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:02.630
Ben hurls an overflowing garbage can to knock
Henry over, then headbutts Victor.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.300
Belch grabs Beverly Marsh’s hair and tries
to slam her into the wall, but she’s able

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:10.160
to scramble away, and Richie uses a garbage
can lid to shield Belch’s incoming punch

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.229
before they all escape.

00:05:11.229 --> 00:05:14.000
I think Henry’s sanity was really starting
to boil after that.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.020
It isn’t specifically written what his reaction
is to this fight, but King does describe that

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.020
Richie was expecting Henry to roll up and
try to beat them up in front of the police

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:25.580
station -- and I think that goes a long way
in conveying how scary and unbalanced Henry

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.580
was becoming.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:30.180
He was already developing this rivalry with
the Losers, but his anger towards them and

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:33.480
his sanity would both snap on one summer night.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.840
Before falling asleep, Henry head voices calling
out to him, and went outside where he could

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:46.090
hear IT speaking to him through the moon.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:50.340
It’s at this point that Henry is unable
to tell reality from his nightmares, so when

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:54.699
IT orders him to kill the losers, he gathers
his friends, picks up some fireworks, and

00:05:54.699 --> 00:05:56.030
sets things into motion.

00:05:56.030 --> 00:06:00.720
On July 3rd 1958, the Bowers Gang are walking
around when they come across Henry’s enemy

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.330
number one: Mike Hanlon.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:06.870
They chase him down towards a creepy abandoned
house at 29 Neibolt Street, and corner Mike

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:10.580
inside the fence, where Henry reveals that
he was the one that killed Mike’s dog.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:14.479
In retaliation, Mike begins throwing rocks,
drawing blood from Henry’s forehead.

00:06:14.479 --> 00:06:18.819
Mike climbs the fence to get away, but Henry
reaches for his foot and Mike kicks down at

00:06:18.819 --> 00:06:22.920
his face, breaking his nose and sending him
into a mad frenzy, pelting Mike with rocks

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:23.990
and firecrackers.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:27.860
Meanwhile, at the junkyard in the Barrens,
the six members of the Losers Club are also

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:31.590
getting ready to shoot firecrackers, but Bill
Denbrough tells everyone to put them away

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.909
and collect a stash of rocks, because he feels
something is about to happen.

00:06:34.909 --> 00:06:38.889
This is likely because Bill has a little bit
of “shine” to him, a psychic and clairvoyant

00:06:38.889 --> 00:06:41.540
ability most prominently featured in The Shining.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:45.789
Henry chases Mike into the gravel pit in the
Barrens where Mike joins Bill, Ben, Beverly,

00:06:45.789 --> 00:06:48.080
Richie, Stan and Eddie in pelting Henry with
rocks.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:52.509
Peter Gordon is the first to flee, probably
realizing that Henry had completely lost it.

00:06:52.509 --> 00:06:56.050
Peter would never return to Bowers’ gang
after that, perhaps because he was one of

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:59.870
the two somewhat intelligent members and he
realized what he was starting to get himself

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:01.080
into… and wanted out.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.720
Henry hits Beverly with a pebble,

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:03.720
"Owwww!!"

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:08.330
....causing Ben to go crazy and tackle him,
and Henry retaliates by throwing a lit M80

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.539
firecracker at him.

00:07:09.539 --> 00:07:13.800
Moose comes in and drags Ben to his knees,
but the others pelted his back with rocks.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:17.389
Victor Criss did the most damage to the Losers
during the fight, perhaps since he was able

00:07:17.389 --> 00:07:21.460
to stay calm and find good rocks, which aided
his already effective fastball throwing ability,

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.879
but in the end, he ended up flinching first
in a head to head battle with Bill and paid

00:07:24.879 --> 00:07:26.039
the price for it.

00:07:26.039 --> 00:07:30.520
With Moose and Belch covered in blood, Bill
threatens Henry to try to get him to leave.

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:34.720
“I think the 6 of us can put you in the
hospital."

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.220
"Seven.”

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:39.419
As he gets away, Henry screams back at them,
"I'll kill you all!" A farewell

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:43.370
that both he and IT tend to use a lot when
dealing with the Losers Club.

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:46.740
Also worth noting, though it may not have
been intentional, Henry kind of helps them

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:47.740
overcome It.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:51.479
If he hadn’t chased Mike into the Barrens
that day, the lucky 7 may have never joined

00:07:51.479 --> 00:07:55.660
up -- and their unity gives them the power
to overcome the manifestations of the monster.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:59.009
After losing the battle that would become
known as The Apocalyptic Rock Fight, Henry

00:07:59.009 --> 00:08:03.259
was hungry to get his revenge, but it would
be another 17 days before their next encounter.

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:07.180
I have to imagine he probably caught up with
Peter Gordon during that time, for ditching

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:10.870
them during the rock fight and spent a lot
of time at the parks in town taking his anger

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.720
out on whatever kids he could find.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.539
Between that, summer school and working on
the farm for his father, I can kind of understand

00:08:16.539 --> 00:08:21.689
why it wasn’t until July 20th that Henry
tracked down one of the Losers: Eddie Kaspbrak.

00:08:21.689 --> 00:08:25.410
They spotted him coming out of Costello Street
Market, and Henry grabbed him before he could

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:26.410
slip back inside.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:29.139
Patrick smacks Eddie in the face and Victor
knocks him to the ground.

00:08:29.139 --> 00:08:32.570
This is all happening in broad daylight in
the middle of town, which is a testament to

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:35.060
where Henry falls on the sanity spectrum at
this point.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:39.700
He pins Eddie down and stuffs his mouth full
of gravel as revenge for the rock fight.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.830
Maybe out of fear for It, and maybe fueled
by his own desire for revenge, Henry’s attack

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.220
continues even when an adult comes out and
pulls him off of Eddie.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:50.460
Henry just pushes the man down and tells him
to go back inside.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.190
The adults in Derry have a tendency to turn
away when bad things are happening, and the

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:58.340
man, whose name is Mr. Gedreax, backs down
from the 12-year old Henry, which I can only

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:02.790
imagine was a horrifying feeling for Eddie,
knowing that not even an adult could save

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:06.560
him, but it did give him a moment to try to
run, at least until a little kid on a trike

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.540
gets in his way and Eddie wipes out.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:12.730
Henry attacks him and breaks his arm, and
to his surprise, Eddie starts laughing, and

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.260
Henry actually looks scared.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:19.090
I think this is an important detail, because
Henry, like IT, seems to be affected by their

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:23.000
laughter, and I’d theorize that these two
evil characters share this common weakness

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.220
because they both need to take advantage of
their victims being afraid.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:30.330
When Eddie laughs, it shows that getting injured
isn’t so scary, and that really puts Henry’s

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:32.690
main weapon, his brute force, in jeopardy.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:36.250
However, when they hear the cop car turn up,
they come to their senses and run for it,

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:38.720
with Patrick spitting in Eddie’s face before
fleeing.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:43.670
Two days later, on July 22nd, Bowers, Victor
Criss, Belch Huggins and Patrick Hockstetter

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:47.050
are at the dump, using a lighter to ignite
their farts and see who can make the longest

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:48.530
flame, laughing as they do so.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:52.170
Henry was supposedly very good at this, because
his father’s girlfriend made beans for them

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.170
once a week.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.480
I think you know the song.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:55.510
After a day full of…

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:59.990
I was gonna say “fun”, but I think I’ll
just say: after a day full of “that”,

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:03.440
Victor and Belch have to leave, so only Patrick
and Henry remain.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:07.420
This is where a new side of Henry Bowers is
revealed, and it’s hard to blame them for

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:09.250
not wanting to put this stuff in the movie.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:13.620
Patrick tells Henry he wants to try something,
and gives him a "hand" as he also gives himself

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:14.620
a "hand".

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:18.340
When Patrick offers to put it in his mouth,
Henry becomes angry and punches him, claiming

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:19.630
he doesn’t go for any of that stuff.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:24.710
Patrick blackmails Henry $1 to keep quiet
about it, but Henry has a counter of his own,

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:28.060
threatening to expose Patrick’s secret:
that he’s been killing dogs and cats in

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:31.170
town and stashing them in a refrigerator in
the junkyard.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:34.960
Soon after, Henry left, worried that Patrick
would expose his little secret.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:39.020
Little did he know, Patrick wouldn’t be
exposing anything to anyone, as he became

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:43.600
the next victim of IT, who kills him using
the form of a swarm of flying leeches.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:47.430
One of the last things that Patrick saw was
a figure, described as having a face like

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:50.290
running wax, trying to decide what it wanted
to be.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:54.560
This was likely because Patrick was so psychologically
messed up, that IT had trouble finding the

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.890
perfect fear for him.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:59.260
We never specifically find out what happened
to the other bullies after that.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:04.780
Peter Gordon, Moose Sadler and Gard Jagermeyer
are not mentioned again, but in 1985, the

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:08.580
Losers do recall that all of Henry’s friends
were killed by IT that summer, but it’s

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:12.340
not clear if Peter, Moose and Gard were considered to be 
a part of that group anymore.

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:16.340
Maybe Jagermeyer was just so dumb, King didn’t
even bother writing a conclusion for him.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:20.270
I had previously mentioned that maybe the
one member of the Bowers Gang who had some

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:24.640
morality and common sense was Victor Criss,
and in early August, I think he starts to

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:27.040
get cold feet about being a part of Bowers’
gang.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:30.950
There’s a truck depot where many of the
kids in town play baseball, and Vic came alone

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:34.070
one day to warn the Losers Club that Henry
was really losing it.

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:38.190
I also think his lack of loyalty to Bowers,
and in turn, IT, was what caused him to become

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:41.930
the next direct victim -- but I’ll explore
that more when we get there.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:46.050
In mid-August, Henry noticed some balloons
on his mailbox, with each of the kids’ faces

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:47.050
on them.

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:51.610
One by one, the balloons popped, and the mailbox
swung down to reveal a package from Robert

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:54.660
Gray, the name used in connection with the
human form of IT.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:58.950
The box contained a new switchblade, since
Henry had lost his chasing Ben in the Barrens.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:02.480
He goes inside, where his father is taking
a beer nap, and the voice of the moon tells

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:04.510
him to push the switch and kill Butch.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:07.010
Henry’s mental state had been deteriorating
all summer.

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:08.010
The Losers knew it.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:09.010
Victor knew it.

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.940
And maybe even Belch realized it.

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:13.400
But now, Henry’s sanity… had snapped!

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:26.540
After murdering his father, the voice told
Henry to get Victor and Belch and go to Kansas

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:27.870
Street that afternoon.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:31.710
When he arrived, he saw Beverly there, and
he heard the voice once again, this time from

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:33.640
out of the sewer, telling him to kill her.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.300
They run after her and Henry catches her by
the hair.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:40.600
Like the incident with Eddie at Costello Market,
Henry defies authority in favor of violence

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:44.600
when a car horn blasts and a woman yells out
for him to stop assaulting Bev.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:48.000
Not backing down, he attacks the woman’s
car with his knife and kicks out her tail

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.740
light causing her to drive away.

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:51.810
Beverly kicks him in the balls and runs...

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:52.810
"AHHHHH!!!!"

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:57.260
...Henry, who can barely walk after the nut-shot
still insists on catching her, which just

00:12:57.260 --> 00:13:01.550
goes to show how violence had become his only
priority, and perhaps how he was being overcome

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:02.890
by the influence of IT.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:06.630
The bullies chase her into The Barrens where
they unknowingly stand on the roof of The

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:08.310
Losers’ underground clubhouse.

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:11.620
Henry knows about the clubhouse because the
voices told him, but doesn’t know where

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:14.050
it is, and he assumes that it’s a treehouse
or something.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:17.190
Belch makes a terrible joke “if they want
a club, I’ll club them.”

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:21.040
I actually find it hilarious, but only because
of how dumb Belch is.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:24.470
Henry and Victor look around by one of the
sewage pipes, where Henry hears the voice

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.010
telling where to find the Losers.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:30.170
The Losers reconvene just before the remaining
bullies show up and start throwing rocks.

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:34.130
At this point, I think that Victor and Belch
are being controlled or manipulated by IT,

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.830
Mike sees them and thinks they are sleepwalking
or drugged.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:40.670
Ben leads them to the pumping station with
Henry, Victor and Belch chasing after them

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:41.670
and throwing rocks.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.890
It’s begun to rain and it’s turning into
a thunderstorm by they time they reach the

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:48.120
embankment where they had previously built
the dam, where they are able to load up on

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:52.020
ammo to throw back at the Bowers Gang, causing
Henry and his friends to peel off to the other

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:54.870
side of the treeline and try to catch them
at the pumping station.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.920
Henry arrives as they climb down into the
sewer.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:59.010
The last Loser to climb in is Richie.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:03.690
Henry slips and falls in a puddle again, causing
Richie to flick him off and yell, “hey banana-heels”,

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.450
just like that day at school, before disappearing
into the sewer.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:10.170
The seven losers stand in a circle at the
bottom of the ladder, and since Henry, Victor

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:14.260
and Belch can only come down one at a time,
Henry realizes he’d essentially be outnumbered.

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:18.290
He throws a huge rock down to scatter them
before coming down, but Richie still bites

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:20.760
him on the ankle before running off into the
inflow pipe.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:24.190
Victor and Belch join Henry, and chase the
Losers into the sewers.

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:27.560
After giving the warning to the Losers about
Henry’s sanity earlier that month, I would

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:32.060
come to the conclusion that IT no longer saw
Victor as a viable ally, and manipulated him

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:34.880
into coming down into the sewers to become
It’s next meal.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:38.110
Like Richie, we know that Victor has been
going to horror movies at the Aladdin, and

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:41.790
I’m guessing it is for this reason that
It takes the form of The Frankenstein Monster

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.060
to decapitate him.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:47.190
It’s unclear if the plan was to take Belch
out as well, but when Belch sees this happen,

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:51.430
he attacks the monster, who easily overpowers
him and tears off half of his face.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:55.880
Henry, literally having tunnel vision, leaves
his friend behind to die with only one focus:

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.050
killing the Losers.

00:14:57.050 --> 00:15:00.990
He never manages to catch up with them though,
and after narrowly escaping being killed by

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:04.160
Bill Denbrough, the monster lets Henry find
his way out of the sewer.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:08.030
The rest of Henry’s summer is not perfectly
spelled out, but given the information we

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:10.180
do have, I’ll try to fill in the blanks.

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:13.680
Henry makes it out of the sewers and decides
to return home, where police are waiting for

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.750
him and take him in for the murder of his
father.

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:19.720
He goes to trial, where he pleads insanity
and they find him to be a psychopath and place

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:21.260
him in Augusta Asylum.

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:25.120
Many of the people in town use Henry as a
scapegoat for the murders committed by IT

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:30.380
in 1957 and 1958, and this becomes a widely
accepted theory despite there being no evidence

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.940
tying him to these other murders.

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:35.240
The fact that the killings stopped as soon
as he was incarcerated and the fact that he

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.260
was found to have gone insane was enough.

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:42.070
Henry would spend the next 21 years in Augusta
before transferring to Juniper Hill Asylum

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:46.550
in 1976, where he would sit and count the
nightlights that burnt out inside of his cell,

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:52.100
until one fateful day in 1985 when Henry would
encounter an old friend.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:04.000
One day, after Mike Hanlon made calls to each
of his 6 childhood friends to let them know

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:08.090
that It had come back, Henry Bowers started
to hear voices in Juniper Hill Asylum, and

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:10.100
he thinks they’re coming from the moon.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.830
He hears the voices of his old friends, Victor
and Belch.

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.450
He hears the voices of the Losers Club taunting
him.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:20.540
And he hears the voice of Pennywise the Dancing
Clown, who tells him to go back and kill them

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.540
all.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.000
Bowers laid awake late one night.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.410
He had seen many night lights burn out over
the years.

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:29.250
They were something that was used to keep
Henry calm and in check, so when his night

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:33.070
light goes out at that moment, it represents
his insanity taking back over.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:35.510
This time, he heard the voice come from under
his bed.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.570
It was his old pal: Victor.

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:39.320
In the TV mini-series, it’s Belch.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:43.240
Of course, it’s not really Victor or Belch,
it’s just another form of It, trying to

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:44.970
get Henry back on It’s side.

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:48.390
Victor says that Henry can hurt the Losers
regardless of if they fear him or not, which

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:50.970
is technically true and lets him out of his
cell.

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:54.840
It uses the form of Pennywise to scare the
guard, Koontz, then takes the form of a giant

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:59.130
Doberman dog, an image that doesn’t play
incredibly well in the mini-series, to attack

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:00.780
Koontz and let Henry get free.

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:04.829
Henry found a steel blade in storm drain,
undoubtedly placed there by It, and hitched

00:17:04.829 --> 00:17:05.990
a ride back into Derry.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:10.179
Eddie would later recognize it as the same
knife Henry had in the sewers when they were

00:17:10.179 --> 00:17:11.179
kids.

00:17:11.179 --> 00:17:14.649
After reuniting with his old friends at lunch
during the day and at the library in the evening,

00:17:14.649 --> 00:17:18.509
Mike Hanlon felt he wasn’t alone as he did
some writing after they left.

00:17:18.509 --> 00:17:23.290
Henry hides out in the glass passageway between
the children’s library and the adult library,

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:26.650
which is symbolic of the fact that he never
really got to grow up outside of the mental

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:30.120
asylum -- he still has a special contempt
for the dark skinned Mike.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:34.050
Mike is only armed with a letter opener, but
he manages to stab Henry’s forearm with

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:34.540
it.

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:37.580
Henry gets him back in the thigh, but Mike
slashes his ribs.

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:41.549
Henry is fat and out of touch, but Mike is
old and much more frail than he used to be.

00:17:41.549 --> 00:17:45.350
He has a chance to finish Henry off, but a
thought pops into head about not wanting to

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:46.620
do It’s dirty work.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:51.179
It takes the form of young Stan Uris’s head
and eggs Henry on, telling him to kill Mike,

00:17:51.179 --> 00:17:54.059
but Mike gets the upper hand and stabs Henry
in the stomach.

00:17:54.059 --> 00:17:58.240
Henry flees the library, leaving Mike badly
injured, but having taken a lot of damage

00:17:58.240 --> 00:17:59.240
himself.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:02.600
It’s past 2 in the morning when Henry comes
upon a sewer grate with a balloon tied to

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:06.789
it, but has to hide away in a bush when he
sees a cop car and ambulance coming by.

00:18:06.789 --> 00:18:11.200
Henry wonders about if Mike was dead yet,
and when the cars pass, the voice of It tells

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.700
him a ride is coming for him.

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:17.980
A 1958 Plymouth Fury pulls up, which is significant
to Henry because that was his father’s dream

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:21.820
car, and it’s significant to me because
it’s the car from Christine, another Stephen

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:23.700
King novel which also has a movie version.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:27.630
I haven’t read the book yet, but I’ve
seen the movie and I expected it to be dumb,

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:30.899
like no point in going to summer school dumb,
but I actually really liked it.

00:18:30.899 --> 00:18:35.289
But back on topic, the driver of the car in
the novel is Belch, or at least a zombie-like

00:18:35.289 --> 00:18:38.240
version of Belch still wearing the Yankees
cap he wore the day he died.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:40.730
I too, hope to be buried in my Cubs hat.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:44.379
Belch doesn’t speak the entire ride, and
most of his nose is gone.

00:18:44.379 --> 00:18:48.240
Henry, clearly not fully understanding that
this is a form of It, starts to feel sorrow

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:50.980
for letting Belch die and goes on this whole
apology.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:54.330
They stop in front of the Derry Townhouse,
the hotel that the Losers are all staying

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:54.880
at.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:58.500
Belch’s mouth opens to cut off Henry’s
apology, but instead of his own voice the

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:01.851
voice that Henry recognized from the moon
came out -- telling him to shut up and get

00:19:01.851 --> 00:19:02.851
them.

00:19:02.851 --> 00:19:04.149
I think at this point Henry understands.

00:19:04.149 --> 00:19:07.559
He retrieves a piece of paper in the glove
compartment with all of the Loser’s room

00:19:07.559 --> 00:19:09.679
numbers listed, and goes after Eddie first.

00:19:09.679 --> 00:19:13.049
He knocks on the door and tells Eddie that
he’s the bellboy, coming with a message

00:19:13.049 --> 00:19:16.090
from his wife, not really knowing that Eddie
even had a wife.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:19.519
This gets Eddie to open up the door, and when
he does, he recognizes Henry stabbing the

00:19:19.519 --> 00:19:20.590
knife in his direction!

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:24.179
He shuts the door on Henry’s arm, which
causes him to drop the blade, but Henry forces

00:19:24.179 --> 00:19:25.179
his way in.

00:19:25.179 --> 00:19:28.879
Eddie smashes a bottle and stabs at Henry
with it, cutting his eye, then his arm.

00:19:28.879 --> 00:19:32.269
Henry pushes him back into the table, but
ends up falling and impaling himself on the

00:19:32.269 --> 00:19:33.269
bottle.

00:19:33.269 --> 00:19:36.600
Eddie’s arm is broken again, but Henry is
dying and the last remaining member of the

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:39.750
once feared Bowers Gang croaks on a hotel
floor.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:43.320
Henry’s downfall highlights the change in
dynamic that takes place after the Loser’s

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.389
Club defeats It in 1958.

00:19:45.389 --> 00:19:48.950
As kids, they constantly feared Henry and
it would usually take a big group of them

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:51.889
or in some cases all 7 of them to evade his
attacks.

00:19:51.889 --> 00:19:56.250
But after the Losers conquered It, Henry became
the real loser, growing old and fat at the

00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:00.230
bottom of the food chain in an asylum while
Bill, Ben, Beverly, Richie, Stan and Eddie

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:04.840
went on to be incredibly successful, with
Mike staying back in Derry to man the lighthouse,

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:05.840
so to speak.

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:10.220
In 1958, Henry and his gang chased Mike away,
while in 1985, Mike chased him out of the

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:12.429
library after putting up a good fight.

00:20:12.429 --> 00:20:16.980
As kids, Eddie’s fear of Henry Bowers was
only second to It, but as an adult Eddie is

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:20.570
able to take him one on one and Henry meets
his demise.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:24.149
So that’s the entire history of The Bowers
Gang, let me know in the comments who I should

00:20:24.149 --> 00:20:29.390
analyse next on Horror History and remember
to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:34.049
week, ring that deathbell for notifications,
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:20:34.049 --> 00:20:35.800
Assuming we both survive.

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:43.860
"AAAAHHHHHH---

